theory.intro:
A rectangular prism is a stack of identical layers of unit cubes. Its volume is the number of cubes in one layer times the number of layers.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3,1.8);
\coordinate (D) at (0,1.8);
\coordinate (E) at (1.039,0.6);
\coordinate (F) at (4.039,0.6);
\coordinate (G) at (4.039,2.4);
\coordinate (H) at (1.039,2.4);
\fill[gray!30,opacity=0.45] (0,0) rectangle (3,0.6);
\fill[gray!30,opacity=0.45] (3,0)--(4.039,0.6)--(4.039,1.2)--(3,0.6)--cycle;
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw (B)--(F)--(G)--(C);
\draw (D)--(H)--(G);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(E)--(F);
\draw[dashed] (E)--(H);
\draw (0,0.6)--(3,0.6);
\draw (0,1.2)--(3,1.2);
\draw (1,0)--(1,1.8);
\draw (2,0)--(2,1.8);
\draw (3,0.6)--(4.039,1.2);
\draw (3,1.2)--(4.039,1.8);
\node[right,font=\small] at (4.3,0.3) {one layer};
\draw[<->] (-0.35,0)--(-0.35,1.8);
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.5,0.9) {number of layers};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
One layer has $3$ rows of $4$ cubes.
There are $2$ layers.
Find the total.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,3);
\draw (1,0)--(1,3);
\draw (2,0)--(2,3);
\draw (3,0)--(3,3);
\draw (4,0)--(4,3);
\draw (0,0)--(4,0);
\draw (0,1)--(4,1);
\draw (0,2)--(4,2);
\draw (0,3)--(4,3);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2\text{ identical layers}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

One layer has $2$ rows of $5$ cubes.
There are $4$ layers.
Find the volume.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,2);
\draw (1,0)--(1,2);
\draw (2,0)--(2,2);
\draw (3,0)--(3,2);
\draw (4,0)--(4,2);
\draw (5,0)--(5,2);
\draw (0,0)--(5,0);
\draw (0,1)--(5,1);
\draw (0,2)--(5,2);
\node[below] at (2.5,0) {$4\text{ identical layers}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

